ERC-1271 smart-account fixture for the ERC-1271 child publish test
(ks256_first_checkpoint_test.go).

erc1271-signer-mock.json holds the creation bytecode and ABI of
ERC1271SignerMock, copied unmodified from forestrie/univocity
test/checkpoints/UnivocityEIP1271.t.sol at commit
879a411614627eb8a56eef34319e278276a6a8ee (lines 15-63). It answers
ERC-1271 for a 65-byte signature its owner makes over the hash it is
asked about. It stands in for a smart-account root such as a Safe,
but it is not one.

Compiled with forge 1.5.1 and solc 0.8.30, matching univocity's
foundry.toml (evm cancun, optimizer on, 200 runs). To regenerate, put
the contract (SPDX line, `pragma solidity ^0.8.24;`, then those lines)
in src/ERC1271SignerMock.sol of an empty directory and run:

  forge build --root . --contracts src --use 0.8.30 \
    --evm-version cancun --optimize --optimizer-runs 200

then write {contract, creationBytecode: bytecode.object, abi} from
out/ERC1271SignerMock.sol/ERC1271SignerMock.json.

